import MoonshineCFSG.MoonshineLRMonsterHeadline
import CFSG.Sporadic.Bridge.MonsterModelsGriess

/-!
# Monstrous moonshine for the Monster, unconditionally, via AxiomMath's CFSG library

`MoonshineLRMonsterHeadline` proves monstrous moonshine for AxiomMath's rational Monster model
`AutO ≤ GL_ℚ(SpaceB)` from one named hypothesis, `GmatEqAutO : Generated.Gmat = AutO`: the group
generated by the visible group `2^{1+24}.Co₁` and the triality element `tauB` is all of `AutO`.

That equation is a theorem of AxiomMath's CFSG library,
`CFSG.Blueprint.NativeSporadic.MonsterModel.gmat_eq_griess`, at commit `5437cdc313` (whose
definitions of `Gmat` and `AutO`, with their 102-file import closure, are byte-identical to those
of commit `69cb972f` from which `VOA/Moonshine/MonsterGriess/` was ported). Its proof passes
through the Stroth–Leon–Sims recognition of the Baby Monster.

Our copies of `Generated.Gmat` and `AutO` are CFSG's definitions renamed, built on CFSG's own
structures `Code.F4`, `Spin.SpinCoord`, `Code.Parker`, on CFSG's Golay code `Code.C`, and on
CFSG's bundled map `SpinLattice.phi0` (the copies in `MoonshineCFSG/MonsterGriess/` of this package). A Lean structure is a
nominal type, so redeclared copies of those structures could never be definitionally equal to
CFSG's; sharing them makes every layer of our definitions (`SpaceB`, `gmul`, `bform`, `AutO`,
`tauB`, `Visible.Gvis`, `Generated.Gmat`) definitionally CFSG's. So CFSG's theorem proves our
hypothesis by unfolding, and the headline theorems hold with no hypothesis.

**How the unfolding is checked.** The kernel accepts `gmat_eq_griess : GmatEqAutO` in
milliseconds. Lean's elaborator does not: its definitional-equality search, which lacks the
kernel's sharing of already-established equalities, runs out of heartbeats on the Griess product
(`gmulX`). So `gmatEqAutO` is added by a short command that hands the declaration
`theorem gmatEqAutO : GmatEqAutO := gmat_eq_griess` to the kernel directly. The resulting constant
is an ordinary kernel-checked theorem; `#print axioms` reports its dependencies as for any other.

This file is the only one in the library that imports CFSG's proofs; the moonshine files import
only CFSG's definitional Monster modules (the structures above). It is kept out of the
`VOA.Moonshine` umbrella so that the umbrella does not pull in the ~20,000-module CFSG proof.

## Main results
* `gmatEqAutO`: the generation theorem `GmatEqAutO`, from CFSG.
* `monsterEquivAutVnat'`: the isomorphism `AutO ≃* Aut V♮`.
* `monstrousMoonshine_unconditional`: monstrous moonshine for AxiomMath's Monster.
-/

namespace VOA.Moonshine.ConwayNorton

open VOA.Moonshine.AutMonster VOA.Moonshine.GriessDictionary
open VOA.Moonshine.MonsterGriess VOA.Moonshine.MonsterAction

open Lean Elab Command in
/- **The generation theorem for AxiomMath's Monster**: the declaration
`theorem gmatEqAutO : GmatEqAutO := gmat_eq_griess`, checked by the kernel alone (see the module
docstring for why the elaborator is bypassed). -/
run_cmd liftTermElabM do
  let name := `VOA.Moonshine.ConwayNorton.gmatEqAutO
  addDecl (Declaration.thmDecl
    { name, levelParams := [], all := [name], type := mkConst ``GmatEqAutO,
      value := mkConst ``CFSG.Blueprint.NativeSporadic.MonsterModel.gmat_eq_griess })
  addDocStringCore name "**The generation theorem for AxiomMath's Monster**: the group \
    generated by the visible group `Gvis` and the triality element `tauB` is the full \
    automorphism group `AutO` of the rational Griess algebra. This is CFSG's `gmat_eq_griess`; \
    our `Generated.Gmat` and `AutO` are definitionally its `Gmat` and `AutO`, checked by the \
    kernel."

/-- `gmatEqAutO` has the stated type (an elaborator-level check of the kernel-added constant). -/
example : GmatEqAutO := gmatEqAutO

/-- **The Monster acts on `V♮` as its full automorphism group**: the isomorphism
`AutO ≃* Aut V♮` sending `g` to the automorphism of `V♮` that acts on `V♮₂` as `g` acts on
`SpaceB`. -/
noncomputable def monsterEquivAutVnat' : AutO ≃* AutVnat :=
  monsterEquivAutVnat gmatEqAutO

/-- The isomorphism `monsterEquivAutVnat'` is compatible with the Griess algebras. -/
theorem monsterEquivAutVnat'_restrict (g : AutO) :
    vnatWeightTwoRestrict (monsterEquivAutVnat' g) =
      griessConj (g : SpaceB ≃ₗ[ℚ] SpaceB) :=
  monsterEquivAutVnat_restrict gmatEqAutO g

/-- **Monstrous moonshine** (Conway–Norton, Borcherds) for AxiomMath's Monster: there is a group
isomorphism `φ` from the Monster `AutO` onto `Aut V♮` such that `φ g` acts on the Griess algebra
`V♮₂ ≅ ℂ ⊗ SpaceB` as `g` does, and for every `g` the McKay–Thompson series of `φ g` is the
normalised Hauptmodul of a genus-zero group containing some `Γ₀(N)` and commensurable with
`SL₂(ℤ)`. -/
theorem monstrousMoonshine_unconditional :
    ∃ φ : AutO ≃* AutVnat,
      (∀ g : AutO, vnatWeightTwoRestrict (φ g) = griessConj (g : SpaceB ≃ₗ[ℚ] SpaceB)) ∧
        ConwayNortonVia (φ : AutO →* AutVnat) :=
  monstrousMoonshine gmatEqAutO

end VOA.Moonshine.ConwayNorton
